From ad59d80a48479ff425a3a14d4fd9150faf3ab397 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:22:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Audit fix b: Miami cards, register, team desk and Team pages

Miami personnel cards (runtime/miami_cards.py): every season's cards are
refreshed through their own date. The yearly statistics block is generated
whole: imported 2002-03 rows kept (added from the league file when
missing), each simulated season's Miami row from closed results plus the
season with every club for split seasons, one playoff row per season and
club from closed playoff results, a coverage line for every row and one
percentage format. Honors come from awards.json for Wade and from the
closed award records (rank 1) for everyone else. Ages at assessment come
from the register's birth date; unsigned draft rights get no role. The
register's contract term clauses follow the contract sheet (Brian Grant
and Caron Butler, 2004-05). Each later season gets a Player_Cards index.

Team desk (runtime/team_status.py): unsigned draft rights are not counted
under contract and have no role; contracts ending June 30 are labelled
after the regular season, with the rookie-scale qualifying-offer note.
Stats_and_Awards/Team/README.md is generated with every season.

Team pages (runtime/write_back.py team_page, period_rows): only players
Miami held under contract in a period are listed; rights holders are named
on not-started pages; an ended period with no game reads complete / No
games. Closed seasons' Team pages are rebuilt by the same rules as of
their stated date. Season Team pages state Miami's playoff record and
link the playoff page (runtime/playoff_stats.py).

Dated register facts (runtime/miami_register.py), forward-only from
2006-06-21: Telfair's PG correction (played games keep SF), read by game
building, rotation reviews, the need score, the desk and cards; carried
by the 2006 rollover. Birth dates back-filled on eight register rows with
date_of_birth_from 2006-06-21 (frozen injury ages stay null). The SF
position guesses in rollover, signing, camp, refill and gm raise from
2006-06-21. signing.league_identity and the rollover identity lookup read
the prospect evidence and the researched births.

team_config 2005-06 records the effective $61,700,000 ceiling with
payroll_ceiling_through_2004_05 kept for earlier dates; gm.payroll_ceiling
gives the same answer for every date.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
